// title: Find Related Emails · Defender XDR
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Defender for Office 365
// tables: EmailEvents
// purpose: The EmailClusterId which can be assigned to a mail is the identifier for the group of similar emails clustered based on heuristic analysis of their contents. Therefore this identifier can be leveraged to find related mails. This is not a hash value of the mail. Once you have identified a suspicious 
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/DFIR/MDO-%20FindRelatedMails.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
let MaliciousEmailCluseriId = "3163234347533"; // Input the EmailClusterId here
EmailEvents
| where EmailClusterId == MaliciousEmailCluseriId
